		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=2351#p2351"><![CDATA[
An updated physics integration of Bullet Physics 2.23 with the latest C4 game engine, version 129. Very basic support for both the Newton and JamesH PhysX test files (included)<br><br>Bullet would perform much better if Cylinder and Box primitives were assigned to the crates and barrels in the PhysX test world.<br><br>Ragdolls and vehicles through COLLADA Physics is on the wish list..<br>It would be good if all Physics integrations are more unified and using a similar C4 interface. If things diverge too much, people can't switch from one to the other physics engine easy.<br><br>Win32 download, includes binaries, Bullet Physics integration and projectfile (17 Mb)<br><a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pub/test/index.php?dir=physics/&amp;file=Bullet_2.23_C4_129_Demo.zip" class="postlink">http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pu ... 9_Demo.zip</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Tue Nov 07, 2006 7:08 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
